Social Media Reject all Accept Selection Accept all Eur.nl Functional Cookies and similar technologies that are strictly necessary for the website to work, such as remembering your preferences, security, enabling log-in or processing forms. Vallonic B.V. Consent Studio CMP consent-studio__consent-id ID of the proof of consent storage within the Consent Studio platform. 30 days consent-studio__storage Local storage for the consent given by the user for certain categories of cookies. 30 days consent-studio__seen Boolean that keeps track of whether the user has seen the cookie banner at least once. 30 days consent-studio__implicit-consent-triggered When a website has implicit consent configured, this cookie stores whether or not it has been triggered or not. 30 days LinkedIn LinkedIn li_gc Used to store guest consent to the use of cookies for non-essential purposes 2 years Cloudflare Cloudflare __cf_bm Cloudflare's bot products identify and mitigate automated traffic to protect your site from bad bots. Cloudflare places the __cf_bm cookie on End User devices that access Customer sites that are protected by Bot Management or Bot Fight Mode. The __cf_bm cookie is necessary for the proper functioning of these bot solutions. Session _cfuvid The _cfuvid cookie is only set when a site uses this option in a Rate Limiting Rule, and is only used to allow the Cloudflare WAF to distinguish individual users who share the same IP address. Session cf_clearance Whether a CAPTCHA or Javascript challenge has been solved. Session Consent Studio Consent Studio consent-studio__* Stores the consent choices you made in the cookie banner. — HubSpot HubSpot hs_sessionid* Identifies your current visit so HubSpot can keep your session consistent while you browse. — Google Google __Secure-ENID Used by Google to prevent fraudulent login attempts. This also contains a Google user ID which can be used for statistics and marketing purposes following a successful login 11 months Hotjar Hotjar _hjSessionUser_* Hotjar cookie that is set when a user first lands on a page with the Hotjar script. It is used to persist the Hotjar User ID, unique to that site on the browser. This ensures that behavior in subsequent visits to the same site will be attributed to the same user ID. 365 days _hjSession_* A cookie that holds the current session data. This ensues that subsequent requests within the session window will be attributed to the same Hotjar session. 30 minutes Erasmus University Rotterdam CMS personalisation.segments This collects anonymous data about which category a visitor fits into. This allows us to offer the visitor content that matches their profile, based on visiting behaviour. — OnlineAfspraken.nl OnlineAfspraken.nl booking widget oa-dao-Resource* Stores the list of bookable resources, such as staff or rooms, that the appointment widget can offer. — oa-dao-ConsumerForm* Stores the layout and field definitions of the booking form, not the details you enter. — oa-dao-AppTypeGroup* Stores the categories used to group appointment types in the booking widget. — oa-booking Stores the details of the appointment you are currently booking. — oa-dao-* Stores appointment widget reference data on your device so the booking form does not have to reload it on every visit. — oa-application-widget-booking-consumerwidget-state Stores technical state the booking widget needs to work. — oa-dao-Mailing-MailingList-* Stores a mailing list that the appointment widget can offer you to subscribe to. — oa-configHash Stores a code used to check whether the booking widget has changed, so out-of-date saved booking data can be cleared. — oa-consumer Stores the identity of the signed-in customer for the booking. — oa-dao-AppType* Stores the list of appointment types the booking widget can offer. — oa-shoppingcart Stores the items you have added to your booking basket. — Analytics These cookies and similar technologies collect information about how visitors use our website, such as which pages are visited most, whether errors occur, and how users interact, to help us measure performance and improve the site. Google Google Analytics _ga ID used to identify users 2 years FPID Registers statistical data on users' behaviour on the website. Used for internal analytics by the website operator. Session FPLC This FPLC cookie is the cross-domain linker cookie hashed from the FPID cookie. It’s not HttpOnly, which means it can be read with JavaScript. It has a relatively short lifetime, just 20 hours. Session _ga_* ID used to identify users 2 years eur.nl Website *__ga_* Keeps track of your current visit for one specific Google Analytics property. — *__ga Identifies your browser so Google Analytics can tell returning visitors from new ones. — *_FPID Identifies returning visitors so Google Analytics can report on visit patterns over time. — *_FPLC Helps Google Analytics keep a consistent visitor identifier when you move between this site's subdomains or linked domains. — *_FPAU Records which audience segments Google Analytics has assigned to you, used for reporting on visitor groups. — Marketing & Social Media These cookies and similar technologies help advertising and social media partners personalise your experience, show you relevant ads, measure campaign results, and enable sharing features. Google Google _gcl_au Used by Google AdSense for experimenting with advertisement efficiency across websites using their services. 3 months NID This cookies is used to collect website statistics and track conversion rates and Google ad personalisation 1 year Google Analytics FPAU Assigns a specific ID to the visitor. This allows the website to determine the number of specific user-visits for analysis and statistics. Session DoubleClick/Google Marketing IDE This cookie is used for targeting, analyzing and optimisation of ad campaigns in DoubleClick/Google Marketing Suite 2 years Google Ads _gcl_ls This item is used by Google Ads to store advertising click identifiers for conversion measureme"
    },
    "https://www.eur.nl/en/working-at-eur/vacancies/data-analyst-project-based-open-research-information-project": {
      "title": "Data Analyst (project-based)",
      "description": "Data Analyst (project-based) – Open Research Information Project | Working at | Erasmus University Rotterdam Skip to main content Skip to search Skip to subnavigation Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Close Open search Close Open menu Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Switch language to EN English current language NL Nederlands Search Close Search Search Featured results Primary Why work at EUR Open submenu Why work at EUR Campus Diversity Societal involvement Sustainability Working conditions Working areas Open submenu Working areas Academic staff Working in Finance Working in IT Working at Legal Affairs Working at Real Estate & Facilities PhD LDE traineeship International staff Practical information Open submenu Practical information Candidate portal Vacancies Data Analyst (project-based) – Open Research Information Project Listen Published Friday 4 Sep 2026 Deadline Wednesday 16 Sep 2026 Work area Research, development, innovation Organisational unit Engagement & Research Services (ERS) Salary € 3.706 - € 5.760 Employment 1 fte - 1 fte Introduction Erasmus University Rotterdam is conducting a six-month diagnostic project on Open Research Information (ORI). The project explores how open infrastructures, including OpenAlex and OpenAIRE, could complement EUR’s institutional Current Research Information System (CRIS), PURE, for research management, evaluation, and strategic decision-making. This is a learning and decision-support project, not an implementation project. Its objective is to provide university management with an evidence-based understanding of what open research information infrastructures can and cannot currently offer EUR. The as-is analysis-covering current research intelligence use cases, tools, and metrics used across faculties-has been completed. We are looking for a Data Analyst to support the to-be analysis: a structured readiness assessment of OpenAlex and OpenAIRE, as well as comparative asessment of proprietary databases for two schools: Erasmus MC and Rotterdam School of Management (RSM). Job description You will work with an existing readiness assessment framework developed within the project. Your role will be to assess and document open databases: OpenAlex and OpenAIRE and proprietary databases: Dimensions, Scopus and Web of Science, against key criteria for Erasmus MC and RSM, including: data coverage, data quality, available metrics, information types, user experience, required skills, required support and governance considerations. Each criterion will be assessed against the research intelligence use cases identified during the as-is phase, such as: tracking research outputs, monitoring research impact and performance, analysing collaboration patterns and monitoring open science practices. Your main activities will include: Conducting structured comparisons between open and proprietary databases, and institutional current information system, Pure for Erasmus MC and RSM, building on existing preliminary coverage analyses Identifying metadata gaps, coverage differences, affiliation and DOI mismatches, and potential workflow implications Populating and substantiating the readiness assessment framework with evidence-based findings Summarising findings in a format that directly supports the project’s management advice phase Reporting weekly to Tung Tung Chan (ERS) and Andrea Tarchi (UB), while working closely with faculty contacts at Erasmus MC (Maarten Engel) and RSM (Brenda de Groot) Job requirements A completed master’s degree in a relevant field (e.g., data science, information science, research management, social sciences, or a related discipline) Strong quantitative data handling and analytical skills, with experience working with datasets, sampling, and comparative analysis Experience with data cleaning, matching, and analysis Affinity with bibliometrics, research information, or open science is an advantage but not required A precise and structured working style, suitable for a short, output-driven project Availability during the full project period from 5 October to 13 November 2026. Employment conditions and benefits We offer you an internationally oriented and varied job in an enthusiastic team, with excellent working conditions in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities (CAO-NU). The start date of this position is 5 October 2026 and you will be based at campus Woudestein in Engagement & Research Services (ERS). This position is for 1 FTE. The salary is dependent on your experience and knowledge and ranges from a minimum of € 3.706 to a maximum of € 5.760 gross per month Scale 10 on a fulltime basis (38 hours), in accordance with the CAO-NU. Your contract will be with EURFlex. EURFlex manages the payroll administration of the Erasmus University Rotterdam (EUR). Employer Erasmus University Rotterdam (EUR) is an internationally oriented university with a strong social orientation in its education and research, as expressed in our mission ‘Creating positive societal impact’. EUR is home to 4.100 academics and professionals and almost 33.000 students from more than 140 countries. Everything we do, we do under the credo The Erasmian Way – Making Minds Matter. We’re global citizens, connecting, entrepreneurial, open-minded, and socially involved. These Erasmian Values function as our internal compass and create EUR’s distinctive and recognizable profile. From these values, with a broad perspective and with an eye for diversity, different backgrounds and opinions, our employees work closely together to solve societal challenges from the dynamic and cosmopolitan city of Rotterdam. Thanks to the high quality and positive societal impact of our research and education, EUR can compete with the top European universities. www.eur.nl . Faculty / Institute / Central service Engagement & Research Services (ERS) advances excellent research and engagement to maximize positive societal impact. ERS creates conditions for transparent, inclusive, collaborative, and impactful research through strategic and operational expertise. We provide pathways for talents to reach their full potential and we advance fruitful collaborations, enabling Erasmus University to be a front runner in embedding excellent research in society. The following areas of support are embedded within ERS: Business Development, Grant Support, Legal Counsels, Open Science, Research Data Management, Ethics Review and Research Intelligence. ERS is a relatively young service department within Erasmus University Rotterdam and is steadily building and extending its service portfolio. ERS provides support to all faculties of Erasmus university Rotterdam (occasionally to Erasmus University Medical Center). Additional information You can find more information about the EUR on our website www.eur.nl . For more information about this vacancy, please contact Tung Tung Chan, chan@eur.nl . Applying Please submit your application, consisting of your CV and a short motivation letter (maximum 2 pages), before 16 September 2026. The selection procedure consists of an interview, invitations will be send by 24 September 2026. We look forward to receiving your application. Persons of all gender identities or expressions, sexual orientations, religions, ethnicities, ages, neurodiversities, functional impairments, citizenships, or any other aspect are welcome to apply and join the EUR community. Stay up to date with new vacancies! Want to be the first to know about vacancies that match your interests? Let us know what you're looking for, and we'll send you an email as soon as a new opportunity that fits your profile is posted.\nDon’t miss out on your perfect job! Sign up Close Stay up to date with new vacancies! Job alert Please select your preferences. When a new job becomes available that matches these preference we'll send you an email. Fields marked with a * are required. First Name Last Name Email address Password Your password requires a minimum of 8 characters of which 2 non-alphabetic Confirm password Business Unit Any Erasmus School of Economics (ESE) Erasmus School of Law (ESL) Erasmus School of History, Culture and Communication (ESHCC) Erasmus School of Social and Behavioural Sciences (ESSB) Erasmus School of Philosophy (ESPhil) Rotterdam School of Management (RSM) International Institute of Social Studies (ISS) Erasmus School of Health Policy & Management (ESHPM) General Management Directorate (ABD) University Library (UB) Convergence Human Resources (HR) Finance (FIN) Education and Student Affairs (E&S) Erasmus Digitalisation and Information Services (EDIS) Real Estate & Facilities (RE&F) Engagement & Research Services (ERS) Marketing & Communications (M&C) RSM BV Institute for Housing and Urban Development Studies (IHS) Any Any Erasmus School of Economics (ESE) Erasmus School of Law (ESL) Erasmus School of History, Culture and Communication (ESHCC) Erasmus School of Social and Behavioural Sciences (ESSB) Erasmus School of Philosophy (ESPhil) Rotterdam School of Management (RSM) International Institute of Social Studies (ISS) Erasmus School of Health Policy & Management (ESHPM) General Management Directorate (ABD) University Library (UB) Convergence Human Resources (HR) Finance (FIN) Education and Student Affairs (E&S) Erasmus Digitalisation and Information Services (EDIS) Real Estate & Facilities (RE&F) Engagement & Research Services (ERS) Marketing & Communications (M&C) RSM BV Institute for Housing and Urban Development Studies (IHS) OK Cancel Expertise Any Administration & Secretariat Policy & Advice IT Marketing & Communication Human Resources Finance Legal Real Estate & Facilities Management Education Research, development, innovation Academic staff PhD Procurement Any Any Administration & Secretariat Policy & Advice IT Marketing & Communication Human Resources Finance Legal Real Estate & Facilities Management Education Research, development, innovation Academic staff PhD Procurement OK Cancel Share this page Interested? Apply now Applicant portal Open navigation for Data Analyst (project-based) – Open Research Information Project Close Interested? Apply now Interested? Apply now Compare 0 study programmes Close Compare 0 study programmes 0 of 3 study programmes selected. @title Duration: @duration Remove @title Compare study programmes Breadcrumb Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Vacancies Data Analyst (project-based) – Open Research Information Project Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Directly to Information Directly to Why work at EUR Working areas International staff Practical information Vacancies Information ANBI Cookies Disclaimer Privacy statement Accessibility Our channels Facebook Instagram X (formerly twitter) Linkedin Youtube Making Minds Matter Watch the video Close Our website uses cookies Overview This website uses cookies and similar technologies (hereinafter collectively: 'cookies'). In this menu, you can choose which types of cookies and purposes you consent to. Functional: ​​These cookies are technically necessary for the website to function properly. Using the website is not possible without accepting these cookies. Analytics: These cookies are used to analyze and improve website usage in general. We take measures to ensure that your privacy is not, or only minimally, affected by these cookies. It's highly appreciated if you toggle the switch. Marketing & Social Media: If you want marketing campaigns and advertisements you see online and on social media to be tailored to your browsing behavior and the interests derived from it, you can enable the slider or click the 'Accept all' button. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time by making new choices in the menu. Click on 'Overview' at the top for a complete overview of the cookies in each category. Please see our cookies page for more information and to reset your cookie preferences. Functional 